WEBVTT

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:13.960
Ichigo...?

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.660
Ichigo!!

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.130
Again... What does that dream mean?

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.750
Ichigo!

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.850
THERE!!!!

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.480
It went over there!

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.840
Bu-Ling, Retasu, let’s go!

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.420
Yes!

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.690
Alright!

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.900
First, Bu-Ling’s attack!

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.360
Retasu-oneechan, it’s coming!

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.320
Leave it to me!

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.790
Ichigo san, your turn!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.250
Take thiiiiis!

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:10.950
Yay!

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.370
Great combination.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.870
Oneesama, when did you...?

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:17.610
We should be such a team during fights!

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.920
Yup!

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:19.880
Hey girls,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.350
we have something to tell you.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.130
If I’m not mistaken, that’s...

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.480
Yes. Those are alien buildings from ancient times.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.320
What you have achieved until now,
the research Ryou and I are continuing,

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.220
and many things we learn from the ruins...

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:44.120
Considering all of these things, we have an
important hypothesis about Mew Aqua.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.710
In ancient times the Mew Aqua was made by the aliens.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.230
The aliens did...?

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.500
What for?

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.780
At this point we can’t tell their goal.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.160
However, if our theory is correct,

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.410
all the Mew Aquas we found so far are fragments of the crystal the aliens used,

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.460
scattered all over the world.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.060
And...

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.460
And then?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.210
What, what?

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:18.900
Deeper analysis suggests that we were probably misunderstanding the Mew Aqua.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:24.400
We assume that “True Mew Aqua” is one huge crystal,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:30.080
though even its tiny fragment has miraculous power, as we all saw.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.860
H-Hey! What do you mean, fragments??

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.090
We don’t know where it is,
but it is somewhere...

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.550
The True Mew Aqua, which stores unimaginable power!

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.260
True Mew Aqua...?

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.120
The aliens don’t know that yet either.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.850
Little do they imagine that the Mew Aqua
was actually made by their ancestors.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.940
However, we can’t let them have the Mew Aqua.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:00.740
I’m sorry everyone, but from now on
the fight will be way more severe.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.090
Hey! Don’t space out!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.350
Shirogane? What... I just had to think about something...

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.330
Don’t scare me!

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.350
I’m sorry.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.090
I didn’t think the fighting would become
this severe... Does it scare you?

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:34.170
In fact, it does... A little.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:37.970
Have faith! I told you
I’ll protect you girls.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:41.150
When it comes to a pinch,
I’ll be your shield or anything.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.600
Shirogane.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.550
Sorry...

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:51.480
Hello?

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.410
Aoyama-kun!

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.500
Now? Uhm, I’m in the café today... so...

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.910
Just go.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.290
The café is closed for today,
and I’ll take care of the rest.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.660
Really? Wah, thank you, Shirogane!

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.710
Aoyama, still there? Wait a second!

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.630
I’ll come over soon like lightning.
Where are you?

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.150
Uwaah, how beautiful!

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.090
A wedding dress, uhm, it’s pretty.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.610
Ah, I’m in love...

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.730
One day I wanna wear one as well!

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:09.020
I think it will look great on you.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.350
Really?

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:10.950
Yup.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.660
Aoyama-kun, I’m so happy!

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:17.440
<i>Congratulations!</i>

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.740
<i>Thank you!</i>

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:22.370
Am I too dreamy?

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.720
Uhm, I can’t believe this.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.110
The weather was so nice
just a minute ago,

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:44.050
and I’m on my long-awaited date with Aoyama-kun.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:46.480
Unseasonal shower, huh?

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:50.900
That’s also caused by the destruction of the environment.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.700
Aoyama-kun?

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:55.450
Ichigo.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.750
Ichigo, are you crying?

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:09.740
No no, Aoyama-kun, it just hit me by surprise.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:13.180
That little thunderstorm is not gonna make me cry!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:18.640
Yes, right. You’re a strong girl after all.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.260
Yup yup! Besides, I’m always happy
as long as with you Aoyama-kun,

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:27.180
even when it’s raining, snowing, or storming heavily!

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.010
Why would I cry?

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.360
I always...

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.640
Always...

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:38.080
I always want to see you with a happy face like now.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:43.590
Aoyama-kun, I definitely won’t cry!

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.290
Thanks, Ichigo.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.620
The rain has stopped!

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.750
True! I wonder, when...

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:54.250
Look!

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.590
A rainbow!

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.220
Beautiful...

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.720
Yes, very.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:21.740
What on earth...?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.880
What’s the matter, Keiichirou?

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.580
I’m getting abnormal signals from an unknown organism.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.160
It’s increasing rapidly.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.090
Is it a Mew Aqua?

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:34.410
It’s still unclear,
but the chances are high.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.540
It’s quite powerful.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:37.180
Where?

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:41.300
Harajuku... around Omotesando.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.180
What a signal!

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.600
That could be...

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.870
This is exactly what I expected.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.830
From the data we gathered, we already had expected...

00:07:55.830 --> 00:08:00.350
...something extraordinary would happen related to Mew Aqua.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.620
Although, I didn’t expect it would be so extreme.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.530
What’s happening?
There’s no wind, but...

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:49.800
<i>These are the images from the sky.</i>

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:56.050
<i>I can hardly believe that this extensive forest was a modern, trendy town until yesterday.</i>

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.050
<i>You heard it right this, is Harajuku in Tokyo.</i>

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.670
<i>Trees are breaking through concrete and asphalt.</i>

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:06.380
<i>There is no explanation so far why these extraordinary phenomena are taking place.</i>

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:09.510
<i>Sources tell us that these phenomena</i>

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:14.690
<i>...have something to do with flying persons often seen recently,</i>

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:18.200
<i>...and with Tokyo Mew Mews.</i>

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.190
<i>That’s it. Reported from the spot.</i>

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:26.730
Keiichirou, anything?

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.280
I’m doing the researching.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:32.360
In this forest, there’s a point from where
extraordinary energy spreads.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.280
We gotta hurry!

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:34.660
Shirogane!

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.330
They’re here.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.620
What’s with those? What is happening?

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:43.060
Keiichirou is researching the case right now.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.530
Maybe a Mew Aqua?

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.040
We can’t tell for sure yet.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.340
There was no sign of this
here yesterday.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.840
You were here yesterday, Ichigo?

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.090
Yes.

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:53.760
Date?

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:55.640
Uhmmm... Kind of...

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:57.180
My congrats.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.760
Congrats.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.890
So impressive. Going out with him everyday? Aren’t you bored already?

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:02.730
Ichigo-san!

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:07.960
When you were here yesterday, did you
notice any strange things going on?

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.760
Strange things...?

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:13.040
Any little thing is fine! There must
have been something different!

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:18.740
Oh, yes! Aoyama-kun wasn’t as lively as he usually is...

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:19.730
Uhm, Ichigo-san...

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:20.940
You should listen better.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.770
Enough Aoyama-kun...!

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:23.430
You dummy.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.640
Ryou, I got it!

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:29.480
There is indeed a huge bundled amount
of energy in the center of the forest.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.210
Huge energy?!

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.760
The Mew Aqua?

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.260
I am unable to make that conclusion.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.390
Anyway, let’s go check it out! Everyone!

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:38.480
Girls,

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.520
if there’s a Mew Aqua, the enemy will try to take it back!

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:43.780
Keep that in mind!

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.910
Mew Mew Strawberry METAMORPHO-SE!

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:01.750
Mew Mew Mint METAMORPHO-SE!

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:07.590
Mew Mew Lettuce METAMORPHO-SE!

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:15.860
Mew Mew Pudding METAMORPHO-SE!

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:22.360
Mew Mew Pomegranate METAMORPHO-SE!

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.890
Ah, I know that place!

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:46.220
It’s a famous toy shop!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:49.880
I still can’t believe this
is that Omotesando.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:52.800
There were many shops I visited often there.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:56.060
Now the only thing we can do here is forest bathing.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.050
Forest bathing, huh?

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:04.410
It’s ironic. This abnormal phenomenon
is actually good for our health.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:12.300
Maybe the aliens knew that the humans would pollute the Earth,

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.340
and that’s why they made
the Mew Aqua...

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.630
Retasu, let’s not talk
about that now...

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:27.380
I don’t know how I can put this, but, we
should hurry and find the Mew Aqua.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.000
A suspicious sound!

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:32.810
A Chimera Anima?

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:41.930
What was THAT?!

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.030
A huge fly!

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.770
F-FLY?!

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:49.690
That means not only the plants, but
the insects also grew bigger!

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:51.940
Hmmm... Then..

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:52.560
Oneesama, your fur’s standing on end!

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.060
Maybe..

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:54.040
No worry!

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.000
Huh!? What’s that sound?

00:12:58.360 --> 00:12:59.890
They are striking back!

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:02.300
Oneesama, I didn’t know you had a weak spot for insects!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.630
Ryou, they suddenly sped up.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:08.790
They’ll reach the target point faster than we planned.

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.180
Is that so?

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.510
That’s the Mew Aqua?

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:23.780
That’s huge...

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:26.350
Looks like something is wrong.

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:28.560
I wonder if it’s real...?

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.870
Anyway, we have to take that thing back with us.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:37.710
What’s wrong?

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.240
This blinking is...!

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.590
Ichigo, the aliens!

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.800
Look out!

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:51.220
Hehe, too bad.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.500
You guys...

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:53.930
Showed up again!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:57.520
This time we’ll get the Mew Aqua!

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.260
Yup, that’s how it is.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.150
I won’t let you!

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:05.780
NOTE: Fu Rai Sen (風雷扇), or “Wind-Thunder-Fan”, is the
name of his attack. It is Ku Rai Sen in the original manga.

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:05.240
Fuu Rai Sen!

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:11.450
Tart, Pie! We won’t let you have the Mew Aqua!

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:14.820
Do not underestimate us!

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:15.450
Tart!

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:17.750
Go, Parapara!

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:29.690
The Mew Aqua turned into a Chimera Anima?

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:31.140
Oh my god! Terrible!

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:33.870
Are you scared?

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.210
What are you doing!?

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:38.850
This might be the Mew Aqua. How could
you turn it into a Chimera Anima?

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.510
Ah, we can do something about that later on...

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:43.030
Go, Chimera Taiboku!

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:45.440
NOTE: Taiboku (大木) means “huge tree”

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:45.440
Beat the hell out of them!

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.570
Not good!

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:55.790
I don’t feel anything...

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.980
Me neither.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:58.710
That’s strange.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.740
He seems so powerful, but...

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:03.210
Retasu!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.720
What? What happened?

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:07.100
Minto...?

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:09.870
The ground is spinning...

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.540
Bu-Ling? What’s wrong, everyone?

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:20.230
What? The oxygen concentration is increasing rapidly around the object.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.760
The oxygen concentration!?

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:29.810
I know the oxygen in the air is necessary for humans,

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:35.060
but if the oxygen concentration is too high, they can’t live.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.660
Hehe, time to finish them off then.

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:47.560
I’m going!

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:50.420
Keiichirou, do you have the dragees
for underwater activities?

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:51.900
Yes, one moment.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:55.830
Please take care.

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:57.930
Each of them works for an hour.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:07.190
Wait for me, everyone!

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:17.910
Zakuro-san!

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:23.790
Now only you are left,
Mew Strawberry!

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:28.080
Don’t push yourself. Even standing
is difficult for you, right?

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:32.260
Hey, go ahead and just
fall down already!

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:40.880
<i>One day I wanna wear one as well!</i>

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:42.680
<i>I think It will look great on you.</i>

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:44.590
<i>Really?</i>

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:45.390
<i>Yup.</i>

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.320
Stop messing with me!

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.830
You who destroy people’s dreams!
You who steal their future!

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:56.160
YOU won’t get the Mew Aqua!

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.530
I won’t obey you,
even at the cost of my life!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.090
Stop being cocky already!

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:04.280
Get her, Chimera Taiboku!

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:13.010
I can’t...

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:15.180
Ichigo!

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.340
Blue Knight...

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:23.270
I knew...

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.760
Ichigo, hang in there!

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:31.230
What’s the matter?

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.650
Keiichirou made this dragee.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:36.650
With it you don’t have to breathe in this air for a while, and you can act.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:40.020
I will protect...

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:40.830
...you.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.090
Blue Knight...

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:57.590
So the Blue Knight... isn’t... Shirogane...

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.710
I’ll protect you.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.130
Ichigo!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:07.390
Everyone’s fine. Counterattack!

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:09.210
In your dreams!

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.810
Go, Chimera Taiboku!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.890
The Mew Aqua has disappeared.

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:20.740
What? The energy is gone?

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:24.560
The energy of the Mew Aqua
can’t be used up so easily.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:25.590
Then that is...

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.480
A fake Mew Aqua!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:31.490
I won’t forgive you what you put us through!

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:33.340
Ok, everyone. Let’s go!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.800
Darn! You’re not gonna lose,
Chimera Taiboku!

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.760
Reborn Lettuce Rush!

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:45.020
Reborn Pomegran’ Spear!

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:48.480
Everyone!

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.550
Ichigo, let’s go!

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:53.520
Reborn Mint Echo!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.980
Alright!

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:56.800
I’ll leave it to you!

00:18:56.800 --> 00:19:00.280
Reborn PuddingRings Inferno!

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:02.500
Thanks! Now the finishing blow!

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:22.930
Reborn Strawberry Surprise!

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.650
We don’t have to stay here any longer. We’re out.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:52.150
If that light, that energy, wasn’t
a Mew Aqua, then what was it?

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:57.590
No idea. It’s gone and I can’t capture any data.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:00.780
It just appeared all of a sudden, that means...

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:02.880
This might happen again.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:06.080
Tokyo will become a jungle?

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:10.890
A jungle wouldn’t be too bad, but
something worse might happen...

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.770
Shirogane...?

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:26.040
Chocolate for my valentine!!

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:27.580
This is the first time I made one by myself!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.860
Will Aoyama-kun be happy with this?!

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:32.220
Why don’t you buy him a
“real yummy chocolate”

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:35.200
instead of giving him that terrible stuff of yours?

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:39.430
What counts is the love I put in.them,
not the taste nor the shape!

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.180
I feel sorry for Aoyama-san.

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:44.210
Oh yes, should I give the Blue Knight some too?

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:45.600
Come on. you’re so fickle.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:46.940
That’s just a “Thank you”-chocolate!!

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:49.840
Next: “The Riddle Dissolves!
The Truth About the Blue Knight”

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.740
Anyway, I’m sorry for them.
